{
  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-pillow-2026-96637",
  "summary": "Pillow: Decompression bomb check bypass in SpiderImagePlugin.seek() leads to unbounded allocation DoS",
  "details": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 13.0.0, SpiderImageFile.seek() in src/PIL/SpiderImagePlugin.py reparses a later SPIDER stack frame and replaces self._size without rerunning Image._decompression_bomb_check(). A tiny file can use a safe first frame to pass Image.open() and then declare very large dimensions in a later mode F frame. Loading that frame allocates approximately four bytes per attacker-declared pixel and can consume multiple gigabytes of memory. This issue is fixed in version 13.0.0.",
